#: ../../../../SECURITY.md:1
msgid "Security Policy"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../SECURITY.md:3
msgid "Reporting a Vulnerability"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../SECURITY.md:5
msgid ""
"To report a security vulnerability, please use the [Tidelift security "
"contact](https://tidelift.com/security). Tidelift will coordinate the fix "
"and disclosure with maintainers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../SECURITY.md:9
msgid "Please do **not** file a public GitHub issue for security reports."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../SECURITY.md:11
msgid "When reporting, if possible, include:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../SECURITY.md:12
msgid "A clear description of the issue and potential impact"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../SECURITY.md:13
msgid "Steps to reproduce or a proof of concept"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../SECURITY.md:14
msgid "Affected urllib3 version(s) and environment details"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../SECURITY.md:15
msgid "Any suggested mitigations"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../SECURITY.md:17
msgid "We typically acknowledge reports within a few business days."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../SECURITY.md:20
msgid "Supported Versions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../SECURITY.md:22
msgid ""
"Only the main branch (the 2.x release line) receives updates, including "
"security fixes. Older release lines (e.g., 1.x) are not maintained. If you "
"are using an older version, please upgrade to the latest 2.x release to "
"receive fixes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../SECURITY.md:27
msgid ""
"When reporting a potential vulnerability, confirm that it reproduces against "
"the latest 2.x version."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../SECURITY.md:31
msgid "Out of Scope Experimental Features"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../SECURITY.md:33
msgid "urllib3 contains two experimental modules: `emscripten` and `http2`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../SECURITY.md:35
msgid ""
"**http2**: Issues in the HTTP/2 module are not considered security "
"vulnerabilities and should be opened as public GitHub issues after checking "
"missing features tracked in issue <https://github.com/urllib3/urllib3/"
"issues/3000>."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../SECURITY.md:39
msgid ""
"**emscripten**: Potential security issues in the `emscripten` module should "
"be reported privately. Project maintainers will decide if they qualify as "
"security issues to be handled through the standard flow or if they should be "
"considered simple bugs and fixed publicly. Issues that would be considered "
"security vulnerabilities in the core package may not qualify as such for the "
"`emscripten` module."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../SECURITY.md:47
msgid "Our Process"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../SECURITY.md:49
msgid ""
"We follow the [Tidelift security process](https://support.tidelift.com/hc/en-"
"us/articles/4406287910036-Security-process) for coordinated vulnerability "
"disclosure. In brief:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../SECURITY.md:51
msgid ""
"Intake and triage: Reports are received privately via Tidelift, validated, "
"and scoped (affected versions, severity)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../SECURITY.md:53
msgid ""
"Private coordination: Tidelift facilitates communication between the "
"reporter and the urllib3 maintainers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../SECURITY.md:55
msgid ""
"Fix and review: We develop, review, and prepare patches (including backports "
"to supported versions when appropriate) and mitigation guidance."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../SECURITY.md:57
msgid ""
"Timeline and embargo: We agree on a reasonable disclosure timeline based on "
"impact and fix complexity; timelines may be accelerated for active "
"exploitation or extended for complex fixes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../SECURITY.md:60
msgid ""
"CVE and advisory: We request and manage CVE IDs via GitHub Security "
"Advisories and prepare public guidance. If desired, we credit the reporter "
"and involved maintainers in the advisory."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../SECURITY.md:63
msgid ""
"Coordinated release: We publish patched releases and the advisory at the "
"agreed time."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../SECURITY.md:67
msgid "Advisories and CVEs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../SECURITY.md:69
msgid ""
"We publish our security advisories on GitHub at [the following page](https://"
"github.com/urllib3/urllib3/security/advisories). We request and manage CVE "
"IDs using GitHub Security Advisories, and published advisories include CVE "
"identifiers (when assigned) and severity information."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../SECURITY.md:73
msgid ""
"To receive notifications when new advisories are published, open the "
"repository page, choose *Watch* → *Custom*, and enable *Security alerts*. "
"You can also enable *Releases* to be notified when patched versions are "
"published."
msgstr ""
